From: Rob Vogelaar <rob.vogelaar@libertyglobal.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 02:40:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] cli: key backhaul metrics by the current link

Reparenting convergence can temporarily leave associated-STA records for a
backhaul STA under both its former and current parent AP.  Indexing metrics by
STA address alone therefore made the topology signal depend on map iteration
order and could display the former link's RSSI on the new topology edge.

Key the dashboard metric by both endpoints: the child's backhaul STA and the
upstream AP BSSID already selected for the topology edge.  This preserves the
normal asynchronous convergence while guaranteeing that a presented signal
belongs to the link being drawn.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 src/rdkb-cli/main.go | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/rdkb-cli/main.go b/src/rdkb-cli/main.go
index 86cb2897..737305aa 100644
--- a/src/rdkb-cli/main.go
+++ b/src/rdkb-cli/main.go
@@ -3285,7 +3285,8 @@ func collectBackhaulLinkMetrics(inventory map[string][]Radio) map[string]Backha
 					} else {
 						continue
 					}
-					metrics[strings.ToLower(sta.MACAddress)] = BackhaulLinkMetric{
+					key := strings.ToLower(sta.MACAddress) + "@" + strings.ToLower(bss.BSSID)
+					metrics[key] = BackhaulLinkMetric{
 						RCPI: rcpi, RSSI: rssi, ObservedAt: sta.TimeStamp,
 					}
 				}
@@ -4973,7 +4974,7 @@ func loadTopologyFromDeviceTree(w  http.ResponseWriter) {
 				"backhaulSTA":   backhaulSTA,
                 "mediaType":     mediaType,
 			}
-			if metric, found := backhaulMetrics[backhaulSTA]; found {
+			if metric, found := backhaulMetrics[backhaulSTA+"@"+upstreamBSSID]; found {
 				edge["rcpi"] = metric.RCPI
 				edge["rssi"] = metric.RSSI
 				if metric.ObservedAt != "" {
